    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31939" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκδῠσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>getting out, escape,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσοδος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.121
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ᾽ ; τὴν ἔ. ποιεῖσθαι</span> to
			make their <i>way out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.109
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔστι Ἕλλησι οὐδεμία ἔ. μὴ
					οὐκ εἶναι δούλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.100
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				426a
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόθεν ἔκδυσιν εὗρες λατρείης
				δοξῶν ;</span> Timo <i><span class="en">
				48
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκλυσιν</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>stripping, deprivation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Man.
				4.331
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
